{# THE COPY CONTRACT — what a zone does to the data, and what it never does.

   It is the first widget in catalogue order on purpose: it must be read before any number below it
   can be misread as a permission. The words are the design's own and are repeated verbatim by the
   empty state, because the two are the same promise made to a person with zones and a person
   without. #}
<div class="c" data-w="lens">
    <span class="tab"><span class="idx">{{ 'PL·43' }}</span>What zones are<span class="src">· zone</span></span>
    <div class="zsec-lead">
        <div class="lens">
            {{ ux_icon('lucide:layers') }}
            <span><b>A lens, not a fence.</b> Zones never gate data — nothing is hidden or blocked because of
                where it falls. They only give every module a second way to group what it already shows:
                “patrols by zone”, “incidents by zone”. Delete a zone and no record is lost.</span>
        </div>
    </div>
    <p class="zrule">Zones <b>never overlap</b> — two of them may run along a shared edge, and a stretch of the area
        may belong to no zone at all. Both are legal; only shared interior is not.</p>
</div>
